  "text": "The cons next: can be rough on digestion. Their fermentable carbohydrates feed gut bacteria, but can also produce gas and bloating. Dry beans take time and planning. Soaking and a full cook make them less convenient than opening a can. They must be cooked properly. Cannellini are white kidney beans, and raw or undercooked beans can retain a natural lectin called P H A. Proper cooking brings it down to safe levels.",
